Hi Mallory,

I think we need more information. Do you need all the data in memory at once? If not, you can try lapply'ing over each file and process them in turns. This might be the best approach, but depends on your analysis. If not, what exactly are you trying to do?

Also, SQLite can be terrific for working with memory that won't all fit in memory at once and you only wish to access subsets of at a time.

Cheers,
Vince

