Oh, I see, you want 200 vars, each of which indicates which rows in df equal that var. This is a somewhat odd thing to do, why not just check for equivalency in whatever you're doing after?

That said... here's a quick and dirty way. Loops can get ugly, fast, because you have to go over the same data over and over again, but this took under a second on my machine.

df <- data.frame(X=sample(1:200,8000, replace=T))

for (i in 1:200){
    varname <- paste0("x",i)
    df[,varname] <- 0
    df[which(df$X == i),varname] <- 1
}

