Hi all,

This week at D-RUG we’ll have a joint talk by Ryan Peek <http://ucdavis.academia.edu/RyanPeek> and Michele Tobias <https://sites.google.com/site/mtobiasresearch/> about different approaches to producing maps in R, including ggmap <http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/ggmap/index.html>, googlevis <http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/googleVis/index.html>, and leafletR <http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/leafletR/index.html>.

For a preview of the kinds of maps you can create with these tools, see Michele’s maps of California Beach Plant Species Distributions <http://micheletobias.github.io/maps/DistributionsMap.html>.

We’ll webcast the talk at this link: https://plus.google.com/events/csq6las4056etldd0t8isauebho. Video and code will be available afterwards.

Best,

Noam
